{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Your loins girded.</b> Readied for the journey." "<b>In haste.</b> A term of alarm and speed, as in ״וַיְהִי דָּוִד נֶחְפָּז לָלֶכֶת״ (I Samuel 23), ״אֲשֶׁר הִשְׁלִיכוּ אֲרָם בְּחָפְזָם״ (II Kings 7)." "<b>It is a pesach to YHWH.</b> The offering is called pesach on account of skipping and passing over — for the Holy One, blessed be He, would skip the houses of Israel among the houses of Egypt, leap from Egyptian to Egyptian, and the Israelite in between was spared. And you shall perform all its rites for the sake of Heaven, in a manner of skipping and leaping — a remembrance to His name, which is called Pesach; and also פשק\"א is a term for stepping."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {2 "the la'az פשק\"א is Old French pascher, 'to step/pass over'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:51:37.014918369Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}